# The guest programs that have no native case, each with the reason its
# checks need a machine of QEMU's (Readme.md).
ahciprobe two disposable AHCI disks, and a KRFFS root on AHCI port 0 by rach2.root=disk
blankprobe the console blanked and shown again, judged by QEMU's screen dumps
blockprobe a root mounted by rach2.fsdisk or rach2.root=disk, and the IDE controller
bootlogprobe a boot line of its own, and the kernel's ring holding every record since that boot
busprobe the IDE driver's two channels and its 48-bit commands
conloadprobe lines typed at the serial console, which the Lenovo lacks
drmcapture a frame drawn for the graphics runners in a guest beside the same frame of the Debian guest; with -p it takes the display as the card's master
drmcompatprobe an i386 program's DRM calls through the x86-64 kernel's compat path, which the i686 build alone makes and the ia32 cases run in QEMU
drmfuzz random ioctls from an ordinary user on the display stack's nodes, which on a real machine are its own GPU's, and vkms by rach2.vkms on the boot line
evprobe keys pressed through QEMU's monitor while it reads, and QEMU's HDA and Sound Blaster models
frag6probe a Packet Too Big that lowers the path MTU of ::1 for ten minutes, for every program on the machine
hotplugprobe a display resized by QEMU's window or a VNC client while it waits, which a running machine cannot do to itself
keylatprobe a key typed on a USB keyboard, and rach2.usblatency on the boot line
lagprobe rach2.blocklag and its companions on the boot line
ldtprobe an i686 program run on the x86-64 kernel, which no native collection stages yet
lockwaitprobe rach2.blocklag on the boot line, and the empty ext2 volume on the root disk's second partition
mixprobe an i386 build at /ia32/mixprobe beside the x86-64 one, which only the x86-64 test image stages
mouseprobe a movement of the mouse made after the open
oomprobe the whole machine run out of frames
orphanprobe grandchildren reaped by the designated init
partsprobe four disks of crafted partition tables, booted with rach2.diskdiag
persistprobe a second boot of the same disk
pure64probe a kernel without the i386 ABI, built with IA32=0 or booted with ia32_emulation=0, which a running machine's kernel is not
sockettest the count of the machine's UDP sockets, which no other process may change
survivorprobe the designated init's exit and the debug shell's return
tlsprobe set_thread_area and %gs of the i686 kernel
ttyprobe lines and keys typed at the console, and its own window and screen
usbdiskprobe sticks pulled and plugged through QEMU's monitor
usbprobe QEMU's USB keyboard, mouse and hub models, and rach2.nousb and rach2.hubtree
musl/audioclientsmusl rach2.audio.loopback on the boot line, and QEMU's recording of its sound for wavcheck
musl/clockloadmusl the emulator stopped by the host and the clocks compared with its time
musl/creddisk three boots of one disk image after _exit
musl/ip6optmusl fixed UDP ports, and a group joined and sent to on the card, eth0, of a machine of its own
musl/keygennoent a processor without RDSEED and RDRAND, by QEMU's -cpu qemu64
musl/punchmusl an empty disk the host formats before the boot and judges after it
musl/saltnoent a processor without RDSEED and RDRAND, by QEMU's -cpu qemu64
musl/sandboxmusl pivot_root, whose new root is a mount's root, as the test image's root is and a private root made by chroot is not
musl/ndwatchmusl router advertisements sent on the card, eth0, and a second ndwatch on it, on a link of its own
musl/procfilesmusl the os-real applets with a held host connection and a known image size
watchdogprobe the q35 watchdog case requires QMP watchdog pause; the Lenovo expiry has its own trial boot in task 78-1b
vgpuprobe QEMU virtio-vga-gl with a virgl renderer and a destructive reset of that virtual GPU
i915gemprobe QEMU's edu device standing in for the HD 4400 by rach2.i915fake, which no installed machine has
gpucompatprobe an i386 program's GPU requests on the x86-64 kernel, under QEMU virgl or the edu i915 fault backend
i915execprobe QEMU's edu device standing in for the HD 4400 by rach2.i915fake, which no installed machine has
i915resetprobe QEMU's edu device standing in for the HD 4400 by rach2.i915fake, which no installed machine has
